 "name_zh": "低保真 Lo-Fi",
 "source": {
  "kind": "groove-adapted",
  "groove_genre_id": "lofi-hip-hop",
  "repo": "gradetwo/groove",
  "license": "MIT",
  "converted": "2026-11-17",
  "tuning": [
   "source selection: groove entry 'lofi-hip-hop' (hiphop.ts): dusty rimshot backbeat, sparse 8th-note hats, heavy source swing",
   "expanded to 2 bars (bar 2 starts as a copy of bar 1)",
   "velocity shaping applied to flat lane(s): rim(37) (grid formula; varied lanes keep source velocities)",
   "bar 2 variation: soft kick pickup at step 30 (end-of-bar kick variation)",
   "swing: groove source swing 30% converts to 650 permille; fixed style value 590 used",
   "fill: sparse snare variation only (no crash/tom; kept restrained for lo-fi)",
   "v2 (2026-11-18): family changed acoustic -> electronic per the v2 brief (HipHop synth base + dark processing); the Virtuosity lofi mapping is not a standalone program (it is an include fragment - parse error as an entry point, probed 2026-11-18). Bitcrusher / vinyl noise floor / wow & flutter have no devices yet: approximated with heavy tape, an 8.5 kHz track lowpass and dark reverb; the missing devices are listed as gap lines in the receipt",
   "Ping-pong delay 0.42 s/mix 0.10 added in v2 loudness/width tuning to widen the synth image (side/mid was 0.016).",
   "D3/D4 wiring (2026-11-19): fx.crusher now drives the real Bitcrusher device (bits 10 / down 2 / aa 0.35); the tape + lowpass approximation above stays as the kit's darkness layer. Vinyl noise floor (D5) and wow & flutter (P7) still have no devices and remain gap lines",
   "D5 noise source (2026-11-19): fx.noise now drives the real Noise Source device (level 0.035 / color 0.85 pink-leaning / crackle 5 per second per channel at level 0.4 / seed 2026, reproducible); the noise enters at the head of the track chain and is darkened by the same tape + lowpass + crusher layer as the drums. Wow & flutter (P7) remains a gap line",
   "P7 wow & flutter (2026-11-19): fx.tape now carries real wow/flutter modulation on the Tape Saturation device (seeded delay-line modulation, same seed = same render). Values are restrained on purpose: wow 0.55 Hz / 0.9 ms peak delay deviation (about +/-0.3% pitch sway with the seeded drift) and flutter 6.5 Hz / 0.04 ms (about +/-0.16%) - a healthy but dusty machine, not a seasick effect. Seed 2026 matches the noise seed above. All other styles keep wow/flutter depths at 0 (bit-identical renders)"
  ]
 },
